# Pendings

Everything carried between sessions that isn't a task yet. `session-log` updates the mention count at the end of every session; `open-session` reads it at the start of the next one. `scripts/check-pendings.mjs` escalates anything that crosses three mentions.

**Columns.** `owner` is who can actually close it — `system` (the project can do it), `project-owner` (needs a decision or an action only the owner can take), `third-party` (waiting on someone outside the project). `state` is `open`, `escalated`, `resolved`, or `dropped` — and `dropped` requires a written reason. `notes` is free text: where a decision stands, who was asked, why it is still here. It is optional and it is the last column, so a six-column board written before this existed still reads correctly.

**Two conventions, and the reason for both.** A working note goes in the `notes` column — **never in an HTML comment**. And a pending is retired by setting its `state`, **never by hiding its row**: the row stays in the table. Both exist because the counter reads this file line by line, and a row it cannot see is a decision nobody signed. Anything the counter is told to ignore is a place where a pending can quietly stop being counted.

